<p>The European Union imposed restrictive measures on 16 individuals and seven entities on Monday over what it called the systematic unlawful deportation and forcible transfer of Ukrainian children to Russia and Russian-occupied areas of Ukraine. The sanctions include asset freezes and travel bans, and the EU said the listed people and organizations were tied to forced assimilation, indoctrination, militarized education, unlawful adoption and the removal of children from Ukraine. The EU Council said nearly 20,500 Ukrainian children have been deported or forcibly transferred since Russia began its war against Ukraine. The EU announced the decision as it, Ukraine and Canada hosted a high-level meeting in Brussels of the International Coalition for the Return of Ukrainian Children, where governments discussed tracing, repatriating and reintegrating children. The United Kingdom and Canada announced related sanctions against Russian targets the same day.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/XehoDPGzL03tNan6I04kU1DEH8GIoe4nE_877Jrj8SSK0OgUSWQcLg7tsN4k5SDrKk7OMjrZCZ2SVhfW2CIrGy4QrFVqw9_8mRHPQW3LXCzpMD8WoxxA4mrjgKM3HBeqk9ZNWBKv2UrySGRHAY4ZXnBFpw7w5txCdXTlr7ROo-NfOaHLiw' alt='Ukraine&#x27;s Foreign Minister Andrii Sybiha speaks during a press conference of the International Coalition for the Return of Ukrainian Children in Brussels on May 11, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Named targets: The sanctioned entities include Russian camps and institutions accused of ideological processing and military-style training, with Meduza reporting that the Orlyonok children&#x27;s camp was among the targets.</li><li>EU funding: The European Commission said it would allocate almost €50 million for initiatives to help identify, return and reintegrate Ukrainian children.</li><li>Coalition size: Kyiv Independent reported ministers from 58 countries announced pledges at the Brussels event, while Le Temps said 72 delegations participated and Switzerland joined the international coalition.</li><li>Commission origin: The Commission said the return-of-children initiative was announced by Ursula von der Leyen in her 2025 State of the Union address.</li></ul><blockquote>Russia is trying to erase their identity - Baiba Braze</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>EU Council: The Council framed the conduct as part of actions undermining Ukraine&#x27;s territorial integrity, sovereignty and independence, and used its Ukraine sanctions framework for the child-removal allegations. (<a href='https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2026/05/11/ukrainian-children-unlawfully-deported-and-forcibly-transferred-to-russia-eu-sanctions-16-individuals-and-seven-entities/'>Council of the European Union</a>)</li><li>Canada: Foreign Minister Anita Anand said Ottawa&#x27;s measures responded to Russian government violations of Ukrainian children&#x27;s rights. (<a href='https://www.canada.ca/en/global-affairs/news/2026/05/minister-anand-announces-additional-sanctions-in-response-to-russias-violations-against-ukrainian-children.html'>Government of Canada</a>)</li><li>Russia: Moscow has continued to deny the allegations about deported Ukrainian children. (<a href='https://www.letemps.ch/articles/enfants-ukrainiens-deportes-de-nouvelles-sanctions-visent-la-russie-pour-graves-violations-du-droit-humanitaire'>Le Temps</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/05/11/eu-sanctions-officials-over-russia-s-deportation-of-ukrainian-children_6753348_4.html'>EU sanctions officials over Russia&#x27;s deportation of Ukrainian children</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/eu-targets-russians-with-sanctions-over-the-abduction-of-thousands-of-ukrainian-children'>EU targets Russians with sanctions over the abduction of thousands of Ukrainian children</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/eu-sanctions-officials-over-deportation-of-ukrainian-c